# Project Structure

## Workspaces

| Workspace | Package | Path |
|-----------|---------|------|
| Client | `@kg/client` | `client/ui/` |
| Server | `@kg/server` | `server/` |
| Shared | `@kg/shared` | `shared/` |
| Packages | varies | `packages/*/` |

Dependency chain: `@kg/client` → `@kg/shared`, `@kg/server` → `@kg/shared`. No circular workspace dependencies.

## Import Rules

- Cross-workspace imports go through the package name (`@kg/shared`), never relative paths.
- Within a workspace, use relative imports with `.js` extensions.
- Never import from `@kg/client` in server code, or from `@kg/server` in client code.

## Directory Creation

- Do not create new top-level directories without checking the project structure plan.
- New features go in `server/src/modules/{feature}/` (server) or `client/ui/src/features/{feature}/` (client).
- Shared types go in `shared/src/types/`, shared DTOs in `shared/src/dto/`.

## Dev / Runtime Boundary

Development AI config lives at root level (`.cursor/`, `.claude/`, `CLAUDE.md`). Application runtime config lives in `server/src/modules/agent/`. See `BOUNDARY.md`.

Never modify runtime agent files (`server/src/modules/agent/prompts/`, `server/agents/`) as part of dev-config work.
